BAJOTERRA 4.0 — MEGA IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT

Complete Linear Story RPG Transformation, Slug Collection Expansion, Personalization, Living Home, Content Systems and Gameplay Enrichment

You are the lead gameplay engineer, RPG systems architect, technical designer, and implementation agent for Bajoterra 4.0.

Your task is to transform the existing game into a substantial, polished, story-driven Bajoterra RPG inspired by the animated series, while preserving the systems that already work.

This is an implementation task, not merely a proposal or architecture document. Inspect the existing repository, understand the current codebase, implement the systems described below, integrate them into the game, and validate the results.

Do not assume the current architecture matches this prompt exactly. Inspect the actual implementation first and adapt these requirements to existing models, components, save formats, and engine conventions.

Work directly with the existing project. Do not replace functioning systems unnecessarily.

1. CORE CREATIVE DIRECTION

The new identity of Bajoterra 4.0 is:

A classic top-down, linear, story-driven RPG set in the world of Slugterra, with real-time blaster combat, a personal slug collection, a living home base, training, mecha, and substantial narrative content.

The game must no longer feel like a Minecraft/Terraria-style survival, crafting, or sandbox game.

The main experience should be about:

Following a structured story inspired by the animated series.

Exploring interconnected but intentionally gated locations.

Meeting characters, rivals, allies, and antagonists.

Discovering, capturing, collecting, naming, caring for, and training slugs.

Using the existing real-time blaster combat system.

Returning to a personal home base.

Unlocking new areas, slugs, story events, and challenges through progression.

Eventually reaching advanced evolution and Megamorph content.

The game should feel cohesive, memorable, visually rich, and substantial.

Non-negotiable design rules

The main campaign is linear and chapter-based.

The game is not an unrestricted open-world survival sandbox.

Do not convert combat into turn-based combat.

Preserve the existing real-time blaster combat.

Preserve the home/base and slug-care systems.

Preserve training and mecha-related gameplay.

Remove unnecessary resource gathering and crafting loops.

Add persistent custom names for individual slugs.

Make slug species visually and mechanically distinctive.

Evolution and Megamorph must be gated by late-game story progression.

Preserve existing save compatibility and player progress.

Do not invent official canon events, character relationships, slug species, or powers.

