3. LINEAR STORY RPG ARCHITECTURE

Implement a modular chapter-based progression system.

The game should follow the broad chronological progression of the animated series, starting at the beginning and advancing through story chapters.

Use story chapters, missions, locations, events, encounters, and unlock conditions.

The player must have a clear sense of:

Current chapter.

Current mission.

Main objective.

Completed objectives.

Available optional missions.

Locked and unlocked locations.

Story progress.

Important discoveries.

Upcoming story milestones.

The player should not be able to skip essential story chapters accidentally.

Allow backtracking to previously visited locations when appropriate, but do not allow unrestricted access to future story areas.

Optional missions should never block the main story unless explicitly designed as a required prerequisite.

